From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: TF_GLM_OVN_OFF_EFFORT_LINE, a thinking-off GLM-5.3 prompt without its default effort line

Ours (2026-11-16); nothing ported. Production's Python engine renders a thinking-off chat by deleting the first literal
<|system|>Reasoning Effort: Max from the template's text (prompts.py thinking_off), so its bench prose prompt is
[gMASK]<sop><|user|>...<|assistant|><think></think> in 33 tokens, where this engine keeps that line and renders the same
prompt in 40. A request that names high or low keeps its line (production deletes the Max text alone), and thinking on
is unchanged.

The knob, a .glm row of platform/environment.zig read where the template is loaded (hf_text_effort.zig, from
HfText.load): TF_GLM_OVN_OFF_EFFORT_LINE=1 rewrites the first `{%- if effective_reasoning_effort is not none -%}` of the
chat template to `{%- if effective_reasoning_effort is not none and (enable_thinking or
effective_reasoning_effort != 'max') -%}` and compiles that. The template is rewritten rather than the rendered text:
a render carries offset-based spans, the history length and the cut flag (model_text.zig Rendered), which stripping
text afterwards would corrupt. The template engine supports or, and, != and parentheses in an if
(core/template/parser.zig orExpr, andExpr, compare, the parenthesised primary), and every render carries
enable_thinking (hf_text.zig renderFn).

The rewrite is what compiles; t.source stays the checkpoint's own text, so templateSource and everything the server
reads from it (thinking_switch, effort_levels, the /api/show template, the keep-state profile hash) are unchanged: the
switch changes the prompt and nothing else. Off, the source is compiled as it arrived, byte for byte. A value that is
not 0 or 1 refuses the load by name, as every strict .glm row does.

Left out: upstream's tests. thinking_request_test.zig pins main's Max line with thinking off (the checkpoint and
effortOff tests) and is unchanged; this switch defaults off, so they pass as they are and the new behaviour is pinned in
thinking_off_effort_line_test.zig (8 tests). One placement note: the row sits after TF_GLM_OVN_HOST_ONCE rather than
after TF_GLM_OVN_KEEP_SEQS, so patches/pr1411's environment.zig and docs/environment.md hunks still apply on this series.

Receipts (2026-11-16). Gates on a shared x86_64 host (scripts/spark-gates.py): the series (tree
c08dd8eade958dd857c180593e0e383e12c7e044, 33 patches) and the stack with patches/pr1411 and patches/cache-salt (tree
e946a74361ca54f02c3baee5437786a1c4dbfe73, 36 patches) PASS against the pristine pin: check-native-cuda-host,
compile-cuda-tests, the standalone host steps and fmt rc 0; test-cuda-host fails only the pin's own cli_config_test
serve --config test (6,832 of 6,866 passed on the series, 33 skipped); lean 341 problems on both sides, 0 new. Mutants,
one changed line each, the tree id checked to differ, each killed by the named test: `!= 'max'` as `!= 'high'` (a named
max drops the line; a named high or low keeps its line); `enable_thinking or` removed (thinking on renders as before);
`if (!on)` inverted (the pin's checkpoint GLM 5.3 off test); indexOf as lastIndexOf (only the first one is rewritten).
Served at TP=3 on three GB10, the image of the stack tree, one stream, three rounds a cell: production's bench prose
prompt as ids is 33 tokens with reply digest 9eb3186f9480; the same prompt as a thinking-off chat with the switch on is
33 tokens and the same digest; with the switch 0 it is 40 tokens and digest 323d3f5bcb55. Decode at 1 2 4 6 8 streams
against the image without this patch, order A T T A, production's prompts as ids: -0.2, +0.1, -0.1, -0.4, +0.3%, inside
the pairs' spread of 0.2 to 0.8%, replies equal.
